Logitech Spotlight (original, USB receiver or Bluetooth) on **Ubuntu 26.04 with GNOME Shell 50 on Wayland**: highlight,
live magnifier and laser pointer drawn inside GNOME Shell, held Next/Back actions, presentation timer with vibration
alerts, battery, per-application profiles and a settings window.

## Install

```bash
sudo apt install ./@DEB@
projecteur-setup enable
```

Then **log out and in once**: GNOME Shell on Wayland only sees a new extension at login. Settings: the Extensions app,
"Projecteur Overlay". The package replaces Ubuntu's Qt5 `projecteur` package. If anything misbehaves,
`projecteur-setup disable` makes the remote a plain keyboard and mouse again.

Check the download: `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS` in the folder with both files.

## Know before you install

An extension runs inside the desktop, so a bug can freeze it. This has been used in one real session (Intel graphics,
one remote) and tested automatically in isolated headless GNOME Shells; AMD and NVIDIA graphics, the Spotlight 2 and
screen sharing in Teams or Zoom are untested. Details: README, section "What was verified, and what was not".
